This is the Assert Statement for the comment "The last index return value must be smaller than the array size."

It is checked at the "LastIndexOf" function in ArrayList.The line of code that has similar assert statement can be located as below:
```cs
int index = Array.LastIndexOf(_items, value, _size - 1, _size);
```
For index variable, we are taking the value returned by Array.LastIndexOf(...), which is stored in the index local variable. For the newCapacity variable, we are asserting whether it is less than the index obtained from the Array.LastIndexOf() method. The OLD keyword is used here to make reference to the original size of the _items array before the method was called.--------------------
public static int Search(Collection c, int val)
{
    int index = c.SearchFrom(c, val, 2);
    // @@@ index is either -1 or greater than or equal to 2
    Debug.Assert(index == -1 || index >= 2);
    return index;
}
